      en: `The National Parliament House was designed by the American architect Louis I. Kahn. Construction began in the 1960s, halted during the Liberation War and was completed in 1982, and the complex is now studied worldwide as one of the great works of modern architecture.\n\nHuge concrete walls are cut with circles, triangles and rectangles that pull light deep into the building, and the whole mass seems to float like a fortress on the surrounding artificial lake. Thin bands of white marble set into the concrete give the facades their quiet, rhythmic order.\n\nPublic access inside is restricted, but the open grounds along Manik Mia Avenue and towards Chandrima Udyan are one of Dhaka's favourite places for an evening stroll. Around sunset the building's reflection in the lake and the changing light on its geometric openings are worth waiting for, in any season.`,
